# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .env.example - the settings that differ from member to member
#
# These values are read on Google Colab from your Colab Secrets, not from any
# file: open a notebook at colab.research.google.com, click the key icon
# (Secrets) in the left sidebar, and add each one under exactly this name.
# Guide: COLAB.md, section 4.2.
#
# Nothing in the project loads a .env file:
#   - on your laptop you need none of these: the notebooks' Colab cell is
#     skipped, and `git push` uses your normal Git login;
#   - the VS Code Colab extension cannot read Colab Secrets yet, so there
#     cell 1 uses its defaults instead (COLAB.md, section 4.3).
#
# To keep your own values on record, copy this file to .env and fill it in -
# .env is git-ignored. Leave GH_TOKEN empty there: it belongs in Colab Secrets
# only, and the repository is public.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where Colab gets the code: your fork (owner/name, as in its GitHub URL) and
# the branch to run.
A03_REPO=your-github-name/your-fork-name
A03_BRANCH=main

# Only for pushing an official run's results from Colab in the browser.
# GH_TOKEN: a fine-grained token for your fork only, with Contents: Read and write.
GH_TOKEN=
GIT_NAME=Your Name
GIT_EMAIL=your-github-name@users.noreply.github.com
